<title>UK: UK's Clarke-Stg strength will be very deflationary.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke-Stg strength will be very deflationary.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Thursday that the recent strength of sterling against the German mark would have a very deflationary impact on Britain's economy.</p>
<p>&quot;With sterling almost 20 percent higher against the deutschmark over the past 12 months, this will have a very delationary effect,&quot; Clarke told Sky Television.</p>
<p>-- Kate Kelland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
